    orcid: ""
title: "HADES: Budgeted Evidence Acquisition for Cyber Threat Hunting Under Adversarial Telemetry"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-08
url: "https://github.com/ftaakash/Hades"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ftaakash/Hades"
abstract: >
  HADES is a benchmark and policy framework for studying budgeted sequential evidence
  acquisition in cyber threat hunting. It constrains the CDB action space to a fixed
  evidence-source menu and evaluates adaptive acquisition policies (P0-P5) under clean
  and adversarial telemetry conditions.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - threat hunting
  - evidence acquisition
  - information gain
  - adversarial telemetry
  - benchmark
license: MIT
